{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires","id":866220,"title":"Neonate Vampires","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-15T19:35:41-07:00","id":866220,"title":"Neonate Vampires","content":"Just curious, but I've been trying to find some kind of &quot;official&quot; character creation for vampires freshly turned. Like, say one wanted to create characters for new gamers. Ideally you would set them up with vampires who know little to nothing about the powers they've come into or the society they've been burdened with. Do they start with less powers, or would you simply apply the same Kindred template and let the powers be something of an experimentation and discovery?<br /> <br /> If anyone can provide a reference, at least, that would be great.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5979-rabidpigmy","name":"rabidpigmy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5979_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T19:53:27-07:00","id":866224,"title":"","content":"Starting characters are neonates, really; their Humanity is largely intact, they barely grasp any Disciplines, they only have three more Merit dots to spend than a mortal. <br /> <br /> If you really wanted to stress how new things are for an absolute fledgling, just have your players not allocate their free Disciplines until they show up in play. Danse Macabre also has some fantastic narrative advice and alternate rules for a Tier 1 chronicle; I remember one of them makes Frenzy harder to resist but much more short-lived, showing how little control a brand new vampire has over the Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 05-21-2016, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T04:30:10-07:00","id":867481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=866224#post866224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Starting characters are neonates, really; their Humanity is largely intact, they barely grasp any Disciplines, they only have three more Merit dots to spend than a mortal.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to stress how new things are for an absolute fledgling, just have your players not allocate their free Disciplines until they show up in play. Danse Macabre also has some fantastic narrative advice and alternate rules for a Tier 1 chronicle; I remember one of them makes Frenzy harder tk resist but much more short-lived, showing how little control a brand new vampire has over the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There was also a great idea of having them start at Humanity 9, if they are completely _fresh_","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:06:10-07:00","id":867493,"title":"","content":"The default character creation is the freshly turned vampire. More advanced vampires start with some EXP during character creation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867481#post867481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There was also a great idea of having them start at Humanity 9, if they are completely _fresh_</div> </div> </div> </div> The book flat out describes Humanity 7 as freshly turned, and Humanity 10-9 as &quot;more human than human.&quot; So, this is basically a house rule that changed what the humanity levels mean.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T05:52:48-07:00","id":867515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867493#post867493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The default character creation is the freshly turned vampire. More advanced vampires start with some EXP during character creation.<br /> <br /> The book flat out describes Humanity 7 as freshly turned, and Humanity 10-9 as &quot;more human than human.&quot; So, this is basically a house rule that changed what the humanity levels mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>The description does not correspond with much of reality. For example, breaking points like &quot;Control someone's mind&quot; etc, are probably things a freshly turned vampire should get a breaking point from... but anyways... as I said - it was a great idea, in no way I meant that it's the rules or anything. It is a houserule <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T06:09:29-07:00","id":867517,"title":"","content":"I'm going to disagree there. Manipulating people is actually something that is very human. Its the basis of every marketing or professional interview. Honestly, I think high Humanity is overthinking an ideal of what it means to be human in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T06:34:49-07:00","id":867530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867517#post867517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to disagree there. Manipulating people is actually something that is very human. Its the basis of every marketing or professional interview. Honestly, I think high Humanity is overthinking an ideal of what it means to be human in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> it's not about manipulating someone.. it's about taking their consent with magical powers, which (almost, and when they do, it's CofD magical stuff) no human has <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:16:31-07:00","id":867544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867530#post867530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's not about manipulating someone.. it's about taking their consent with magical powers, which (almost, and when they do, it's CofD magical stuff) no human has <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting distinction, but begs some followup questions:<ul><li>Where would you put blackmail on the scale?</li> <li>Would you apply a penalty/bonus to a violence-based breaking point depending on if the character used Vigor/Celerity to commit the violence or not?</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:25:47-07:00","id":867547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867544#post867544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's an interesting distinction, but begs some followup questions:<ul><li>Where would you put blackmail on the scale?</li> <li>Would you apply a penalty/bonus to a violence-based breaking point depending on if the character used Vigor/Celerity to commit the violence or not?</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Blackmail - I wouldnt.<br /> <br /> Physical Disciplines - Depends on context? Let's not forget that Vigor gives you weapon quality.. which crushes bones and is definitely something which would snap at the person &quot;you're no longer just a human&quot;, same thing with Celerity, where you're able to move far in a blink of an eye. For most people, these might be _even_ more jarring, as most people is at least in social situations almost daily, and thus relating to words might be easier.. where most of us don't get into fights that often, and suddenly you can break bones with a punch.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T07:35:39-07:00","id":867551,"title":"","content":"The use of magical powers is really not included in the Humanity list - if it was, then merely displaying Celerity, Vigor, or Protean should be a breaking point. They're not listed as a sample. So, unless your ST rules otherwise, the mere fact you have magical powers, and can use them, is not a breaking point. Which leads me to conclude that the reason for the breaking point is violating another human rather than the fact its supernatural manipulation.<br /> <br /> You're drawing the line based on magical powers or not. I don't think that's what those points represent. That's why its entirely arguable. Because your'e drawing conclusions that I simply don't agree with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:40:47-07:00","id":867700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/866220-neonate-vampires?p=867551#post867551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The use of magical powers is really not included in the Humanity list - if it was, then merely displaying Celerity, Vigor, or Protean should be a breaking point. They're not listed as a sample. So, unless your ST rules otherwise, the mere fact you have magical powers, and can use them, is not a breaking point. Which leads me to conclude that the reason for the breaking point is violating another human rather than the fact its supernatural manipulation.<br /> <br /> You're drawing the line based on magical powers or not. I don't think that's what those points represent. That's why its entirely arguable. Because your'e drawing conclusions that I simply don't agree with.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are in several instances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T13:28:57-07:00","id":867781,"title":"","content":"The text does call them sample breaking points and does say the list is not exhaustive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}